@startuml
title Multithreaded Data Acquisition Pipeline - Component Diagram

left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle uml2

component "Pipeline CLI\n<<external driver>>" as CLI

component "Multithreaded Data Acquisition Pipeline" as Pipeline {
  component "ioPipelineController" as Controller
  component "ioUsbReadController\n<<producer>>" as ReadWorker
  queue "ioDataBuffer\n<<shared buffer>>" as Buffer
  component "ioUsbWriteController\n<<consumer>>" as WriteWorker

  component "ioFileInputByteStream" as FileInput
  component "ioFtdiByteStream" as FtdiInput
  component "ioFileByteStream" as FileSink
  component "ioFtdiOutputByteStream" as FtdiSink

  () "pipelineLifecycle" as PipelineLifecycle
  () "readerControl" as ReaderControl
  () "writerControl" as WriterControl
  () "ioReadableByteStream" as ReadableContract
  () "bufferWriter" as BufferWriter
  () "bufferReader" as BufferReader
  () "ioWritableByteStream" as WritableContract
}

PipelineLifecycle - Controller
ReaderControl - ReadWorker
WriterControl - WriteWorker
ReadableContract - FileInput
ReadableContract - FtdiInput
BufferWriter - Buffer
BufferReader - Buffer
WritableContract - FileSink
WritableContract - FtdiSink

CLI ..> PipelineLifecycle : start() / stop() / join()
Controller ..> ReaderControl : configure reader
Controller ..> WriterControl : configure writer
Controller ..> ReadableContract : select input mode
Controller ..> WritableContract : select output mode

ReadWorker ..> ReadableContract : read_bytes()
ReadWorker ..> BufferWriter : push() / close()
WriteWorker ..> BufferReader : pop()
WriteWorker ..> WritableContract : write_bytes()

note bottom of Pipeline
The component view focuses on software contracts:
the controller coordinates workers, the workers
depend on stream interfaces, and the buffer exposes
separate producer and consumer entry points.
end note

note bottom of Buffer
ioDataBuffer is shared by both workers.
It is not owned by either worker component.
end note
@enduml
